A Pirate Looks at 40
Tabbed by:Matt Jones

Jack Johnson's version is faithful to the original in terms of chord progression,
but instead of a full band playing (and strumming the chords) it's just Jack
and his guitar. One of the main differences in the two versions is Jack leaves
off the last two verses (finishes with "just a few friends") wheras Jimmy keeps going.
Any way you square it though, this is a great song and easy to play.

Chord Progression:
[G] [C] [G] [Am] [D] [G]

